	Here’s a very simple but coherent algo you can implement right now with what you have:
	2.1 Regime score from entropy
	Take your entropy vector (e.g. tick entropy at 1s, 5s, 10s, 30s, 1m, 5m, 15m) and compress to a scalar:
	R(t) = normalized_entropy_short_term  (e.g. 1s–30s average, scaled to [0,1])
	Then define:
	Low entropy: R(t) <= θ_low (e.g. bottom 30% of historical values)
	High entropy: R(t) >= θ_high (e.g. top 40%)
	In between → do nothing / de-risk
	You can calibrate θ_low, θ_high from historical distribution (no new features needed).
	2.2 Directional bias from existing features
	Use your existing signals for direction:
	imbalance = PWI(0–20%) or some linear combo of PWI levels
	aggr_imb = aggr_buy_vol - aggr_sell_vol over last X seconds
	mom = short_term_price_momentum (you already compute)
	Then define, for example:
	bull_score  = w1 * norm(PWI_bid_side) + w2 * norm(aggr_imb) + w3 * norm(mom)
	bear_score  = w1 * norm(PWI_ask_side) - w2 * norm(aggr_imb) - w3 * norm(mom)
	signal      = bull_score - bear_score   # >0 bullish, <0 bearish
	Even a very simple:
	signal > +S_thresh → long
	signal < -S_thresh → short
	is fine for v0.1.
	All of that uses features you already have.
	2.3 Trading logic (momentum only, entropy-gated)
	State: position, entry_price, time_in_trade.
	Entry (flat → open)
	Condition:
	entropy_low == true
	|signal| > S_thresh
	If signal > 0 → open long
	If signal < 0 → open short
	Size: size = base_notional / volatility or just fixed small size
	Exit (in a position)
	Use only stuff you already have:
	Time stop: exit after T_max seconds since entry
	Price stop:
	TP at +k_tp * σ from entry
	SL at -k_sl * σ from entry
	(σ = your realized volatility feature)
	Entropy regime change:
	If regime flips to high entropy, close the momentum trade (assume trend edge is gone).
	No MM, no RL, no new features needed.


